    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1820">

                <pb facs="1465" n="1349" sameAs="frus:frus1912/pg1349"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 367.11/28.</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The American Ambassador to Great
                            Britain to the Secretary of
                    State</hi>.</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.—Paraphrase.]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">American Embassy</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">London</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1912-11-11">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">November 11, 1912</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>The British Ambassador at Constantinople reports to the Foreign Office that
                    arrangements have been made to accommodate bona fide, American citizens at
                    Constantinople in case of need on board IT. M. S. <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Weymouth;</hi> protection at other ports is now being arranged for, and
                    would be extended, as Sir Edward Grey understands, in conjunction with other
                    Powers.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Reid.</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
